WEBVTT

00:07.632 --> 00:09.300
There is nothing to fear.

00:10.885 --> 00:15.682
If you lose your memory of magic,
you'll forget the fear of it as well.

00:16.641 --> 00:19.269
You will just become an Outsider.

00:19.352 --> 00:21.229
I told you it wasn't us.

00:21.312 --> 00:23.565
Why won't you listen?

00:24.149 --> 00:26.568
No. Please, no.

00:44.169 --> 00:45.462
This is...

00:45.545 --> 00:47.297
Serpent's Bed of Sand?

00:47.881 --> 00:50.300
Agott was trying to explain,

00:50.383 --> 00:52.510
but you didn't listen. You're terrible!

00:53.428 --> 00:54.512
Who are they?

00:55.180 --> 00:56.264
They're children.

00:56.973 --> 00:58.683
They burned the flag.

01:00.727 --> 01:01.895
Me too.

01:02.479 --> 01:06.649
Adults who treat “kids” like
they’re some kind of species...

01:07.484 --> 01:08.651
I hate that.

01:08.735 --> 01:11.154
What matters isn’t the circumstances.

01:12.072 --> 01:14.449
It’s the fact that a rule was broken.

01:15.825 --> 01:18.161
The order and peace of this world

01:18.244 --> 01:22.957
are upheld only because every witch
strictly follows the code.

01:24.000 --> 01:26.211
One crack is all it takes to fall apart.

01:26.753 --> 01:30.256
And hence, there can be no exceptions.

01:30.757 --> 01:33.176
You refuse to listen to the kids,

01:33.259 --> 01:35.386
and yet you sure have a lot to say.

01:37.764 --> 01:41.935
Don't lay a hand on my apprentice,
Easthies.

01:43.019 --> 01:43.937
I see.

01:44.479 --> 01:46.314
So it's your apprentice.

01:47.232 --> 01:49.943
No wonder. As arrogant as their master.

01:51.402 --> 01:54.572
If being like you is a model student,
then screw that.

01:55.990 --> 01:59.077
Especially if this is what
the Knights Moralis calls their job.

02:01.162 --> 02:04.082
We only want to protect order.

02:05.708 --> 02:09.254
Magic powerful enough to reshape the land,

02:09.337 --> 02:12.090
like the Dadah Range
and the Forest of Thristas,

02:12.173 --> 02:14.551
that's war magic from before
the Day of the Pact.

02:16.261 --> 02:18.972
If something like that’s been cast
in this era,

02:19.472 --> 02:22.142
then of course it has to be dealt with.

02:22.684 --> 02:24.018
Even so,

02:24.102 --> 02:27.355
it’s not right to strip someone’s
memories without hearing them out.

02:27.981 --> 02:29.107
And besides,

02:29.190 --> 02:32.193
I don’t recall ever giving
my apprentices the skills or the tools

02:32.735 --> 02:35.113
to pull off magic of this scale.

02:36.072 --> 02:37.740
Even if you hadn't,

02:37.824 --> 02:40.243
is it possible
the Brimmed Caps could have?

02:45.707 --> 02:47.333
Hey, you guys!

02:47.834 --> 02:50.295
Argue all you want,

02:50.378 --> 02:53.631
but have you forgotten
what witches are meant to do?

02:53.715 --> 02:56.134
"Bring the blessings
of magic to the people."

02:56.801 --> 02:59.721
They understand that a lot better
than you do.

03:02.473 --> 03:05.560
Quit standing around. All of you help out.

03:05.643 --> 03:07.937
You've got those handy flags, don't you?

03:16.196 --> 03:18.489
Will that actually fix it?

03:18.573 --> 03:20.992
No, I just stopped the bleeding.

03:21.075 --> 03:22.785
I'll carry him to Kalhn like this.

03:23.286 --> 03:26.206
If we get her to a doctor right away,
her life won’t be in dang--

03:26.289 --> 03:30.418
I saw it. You used magic to fix that flag,
didn't you?!

03:31.878 --> 03:34.088
You can heal this child's injuries too,
can't you?

03:34.172 --> 03:37.050
Magic should have that ability!

03:38.801 --> 03:40.845
No, it doesn't.

03:41.596 --> 03:42.805
But...

03:43.306 --> 03:44.557
but that can't be!

03:44.641 --> 03:45.850
Let go of me.

03:49.395 --> 03:51.940
Or should I stop carrying him?

03:57.320 --> 03:58.321
I'm sorry.

04:00.073 --> 04:02.951
Please take care of him.

04:04.827 --> 04:05.995
Seal off the area.

04:06.079 --> 04:08.498
Don't let anyone
other than witches inside.

04:09.832 --> 04:11.542
Once the Outsiders are gone,

04:13.002 --> 04:15.255
we'll conduct a full investigation.

05:50.558 --> 05:54.520
UNDER THE SUSPICION OF KNIGHTS MORALIS

05:58.900 --> 06:01.444
Just basic, fundamental magic.

06:02.153 --> 06:05.114
No way this would bring down
an entire riverbank.

06:05.615 --> 06:06.699
Yeah.

06:09.369 --> 06:10.328
Show me your hands.

06:12.622 --> 06:17.085
The Brimmed Caps sometimes carve seals
into their bodies as tattoos.

06:17.919 --> 06:21.839
Forbidden magic that enhances
or alters the body,

06:21.923 --> 06:23.841
amplifying magical power.

06:26.594 --> 06:30.306
Fresh pen calluses
and hands stained with conjuring ink.

06:38.064 --> 06:39.565
That's enough, isn't it?

06:44.946 --> 06:49.117
Once we report this to the Great Hall,
we'll begin an investigation.

06:49.742 --> 06:52.954
And if it turns out
you really did cause this,

06:53.037 --> 06:54.622
we won't show any mercy.

06:55.206 --> 06:57.250
Don't lose what you've just learned.

06:57.333 --> 06:59.544
You'd better be careful.

07:08.177 --> 07:10.346
Wow, that was nerve-wracking.

07:10.430 --> 07:12.640
I'm just glad everyone's okay.

07:16.310 --> 07:19.188
We adults shouldn’t have left you alone.

07:19.689 --> 07:20.940
I'm so sorry.

07:21.023 --> 07:23.401
It's not your fault, Master.

07:23.484 --> 07:26.446
Even still, Agott and Coco,

07:28.281 --> 07:31.409
I want you to understand
just how dangerous that was.

07:32.201 --> 07:34.912
If anyone had discovered
the secret of magic,

07:35.746 --> 07:39.792
we would've had to erase the memories
of everyone we helped.

07:40.585 --> 07:42.670
A person’s memories are their entire life.

07:43.171 --> 07:46.174
Your actions put something like that
in the balance.

07:46.757 --> 07:48.092
We're sorry.

07:48.176 --> 07:49.677
We'll be more careful.

07:50.887 --> 07:51.804
This...

07:52.805 --> 07:55.308
probably set my exam back.

07:55.892 --> 07:58.060
But you pulled it off.

07:58.561 --> 07:59.395
And so

07:59.896 --> 08:03.566
I'll put in a request for you
to take the second exam, Agott.

08:05.443 --> 08:06.319
If you pass,

08:06.402 --> 08:09.947
you'll be recognized as capable
of accompanying real field work.

08:11.491 --> 08:13.618
No using magic in front of others
until then.

08:13.701 --> 08:15.203
Can you promise me that?

08:15.286 --> 08:18.080
Oh, yes!

08:18.164 --> 08:20.541
What?! Only Agott?

08:20.625 --> 08:23.085
Master! What about us?

08:23.169 --> 08:27.507
You still haven’t finished drawing out
the entire basic magic textbook, have you?

08:27.590 --> 08:28.674
Ugh!

08:28.758 --> 08:31.427
I don't like exams so I don't care.

08:31.511 --> 08:33.596
There are other exams?!

08:34.931 --> 08:36.307
Hey, Qifrey.

08:37.225 --> 08:38.351
You sure about this?

08:38.434 --> 08:40.811
You were worried Agott
was rushing into things.

08:41.312 --> 08:42.230
Yes.

08:42.313 --> 08:43.356
But...

08:45.358 --> 08:46.817
not anymore.

08:48.319 --> 08:51.822
So then I figured I should trust them.

08:52.823 --> 08:54.200
You're way too soft.

08:54.283 --> 08:57.578
That's what happens when you've got
students who are hard on themselves.

08:58.829 --> 09:00.248
Master Qifrey,

09:01.123 --> 09:03.376
I want to go back and practice already.

09:03.459 --> 09:04.502
Hold on.

09:10.675 --> 09:13.469
There's one more thing we need to do.

09:14.345 --> 09:17.265
That girl was Qifrey's new apprentice, right?

09:18.015 --> 09:19.517
If the rumors are true...

09:21.102 --> 09:23.771
Can you prove the rumors are true?

09:23.854 --> 09:25.064
No.

09:25.565 --> 09:28.609
There's no way to find evidence
in that petrified house.

09:30.069 --> 09:34.282
Then we'll have to make her confess. Look.

09:35.283 --> 09:39.120
Because of that magic, the river
downstream is starting to dry up.

09:39.829 --> 09:43.249
A single rockfall can collapse the bank,
shift the current,

09:43.332 --> 09:45.459
and force everything downstream to change.

09:46.627 --> 09:49.046
Just like that,
the beautiful landscape that once was

09:49.714 --> 09:52.174
is lost forever.

09:54.552 --> 09:56.971
That girl is the first falling stone.

09:57.471 --> 09:59.849
If there's even a chance
she'll set things in motion,

09:59.932 --> 10:02.560
we have to remove her, no matter what.

10:02.643 --> 10:05.062
Whoa!

10:07.148 --> 10:09.358
Olruggio's pen is a special one.

10:09.900 --> 10:11.902
It's called a Searneedle wand.

10:11.986 --> 10:15.323
It can burn seals into stone and wood.

10:17.158 --> 10:18.826
It's just a temporary fix though.

10:34.759 --> 10:36.802
The river's starting to flow again.

10:37.386 --> 10:39.930
Looks like the sand-dust spell
is wearing off.

10:53.277 --> 10:54.904
Here, you dropped something.

10:56.280 --> 10:57.573
Be careful.

10:57.657 --> 11:00.618
Don’t forget your hat
or your conjuring ink.

11:02.411 --> 11:05.456
I'm sorry! Thank you.

11:08.501 --> 11:10.127
Huh? That's strange.

11:12.213 --> 11:14.674
My conjuring ink hasn't gone down at all!

11:16.967 --> 11:19.053
Are the vials magic or something?

11:19.136 --> 11:21.097
Like it just keeps refilling forever?

11:21.180 --> 11:24.016
Coco, could I take a look at that?

11:24.892 --> 11:26.143
Master?

11:38.364 --> 11:41.951
Magic is a “falsehood”
that colors the world.

11:43.953 --> 11:46.914
Even though the hands
that paint beautiful magic

11:46.997 --> 11:50.042
get stained with ink.

11:52.878 --> 11:54.046
Lies...

11:56.632 --> 11:59.051
they fall apart the closer you get.

12:08.310 --> 12:10.980
How long do you think
you can keep it hidden?

12:16.026 --> 12:17.778
This ink,

12:18.821 --> 12:21.490
you got it
from Mr. Nolnoa in Kalhn, right?

12:21.574 --> 12:22.450
Yes.

12:28.164 --> 12:29.707
- Wow.
- Olruggio.

12:29.790 --> 12:32.418
Take everyone back
to the atelier ahead of me.

12:33.919 --> 12:36.088
Where are you going?

12:36.172 --> 12:37.089
I...

12:39.133 --> 12:42.678
missed my chance to buy Coco a pen
during all the commotion the other day.

12:43.179 --> 12:46.265
It's close, so I'll stop by Kalhn first.

12:46.348 --> 12:48.559
Then I want Silvernectar wine.

12:49.059 --> 12:51.437
Then one early-pressed and one aged.

12:51.520 --> 12:53.272
Got it. Leave it to me.

12:54.064 --> 12:54.940
I'm sorry.

12:58.152 --> 13:01.572
There’s something I need to confirm.

13:08.120 --> 13:11.540
Huh? The door is gone.

13:12.208 --> 13:13.793
Oh shoot.

13:14.376 --> 13:16.295
Looks like the shop is closed today.

13:16.378 --> 13:19.548
Wait, when it’s closed,
the whole shop disappears?!

13:22.259 --> 13:24.303
Oh, Mr. Qifrey!

13:25.679 --> 13:27.556
And the girl from the other day.

13:28.140 --> 13:29.183
Tartah.

13:29.683 --> 13:30.643
Thank goodness.

13:30.726 --> 13:32.561
I need to see Mr. Nolnoa.

13:32.645 --> 13:35.064
Oh, hang on a sec.

13:52.706 --> 13:54.667
Please, come in.

14:01.590 --> 14:04.093
This room's completely different
from last time.

14:05.678 --> 14:09.223
Of course it is. The room changes
depending on the doorknob.

14:10.182 --> 14:12.101
Gramps is probably on the third floor.

14:12.685 --> 14:14.728
Thanks. Sorry to intrude.

14:15.563 --> 14:17.356
Oh, uh,

14:18.065 --> 14:19.149
hold on.

14:20.150 --> 14:22.611
Um, your name...

14:23.279 --> 14:24.238
It's Coco.

14:24.738 --> 14:25.865
I'm Coco.

14:27.241 --> 14:30.160
That cut on your right foot.
You should disinfect it right away.

14:31.412 --> 14:32.454
Come on, back here.

14:32.955 --> 14:35.374
I've got some Tranquileaf.
I'll patch you up.

14:43.841 --> 14:46.510
There are so many tools I don’t recognize.

14:50.806 --> 14:53.392
Wow, so pretty.

14:54.268 --> 14:56.645
What are all these
different colored powders?

14:56.729 --> 14:58.898
Try not to mess with them too much.

14:58.981 --> 15:00.983
It’s a problem if they get disarranged.

15:02.151 --> 15:04.111
They're magical dyes.

15:04.194 --> 15:07.615
Additives used to enhance
the effects of conjuring ink.

15:10.200 --> 15:11.327
Mr. Nolnoa.

15:13.537 --> 15:15.331
Today, the shop is closed.

15:15.414 --> 15:16.332
Yes.

15:16.957 --> 15:18.083
But...

15:19.168 --> 15:20.628
I'm just kidding.

15:20.711 --> 15:23.422
I know why you’re here.

15:24.590 --> 15:28.469
It’s about the seal drawn on
the alley tiles, isn’t it?

15:29.303 --> 15:31.847
I still haven’t figured anything out.

15:32.348 --> 15:35.726
I tried spells to separate
the different magic dyes,

15:36.477 --> 15:39.271
but they’d all melted together
beautifully.

15:39.897 --> 15:42.483
Have you found something?

15:42.566 --> 15:45.819
Actually, I came across something.

15:58.707 --> 16:01.210
This is similar.

16:01.835 --> 16:05.589
No, even that faint bluish tint
is exactly the same.

16:07.257 --> 16:09.551
Where did you get this?

16:12.054 --> 16:13.097
Wait a second.

16:13.806 --> 16:15.349
Isn't this my vial?

16:17.101 --> 16:18.519
It was that day.

16:19.311 --> 16:22.856
The Brimmed Cap must have cast
a spell on the bottle then.

16:25.192 --> 16:26.443
What are you doing?

16:27.444 --> 16:30.614
Before you draw anything,
you should examine that ink first.

16:35.285 --> 16:39.498
Hey, what’s that pale blue dye called?

16:40.082 --> 16:42.501
The big one up near the ceiling!

16:42.584 --> 16:45.212
That's powdered Azuremoon Flower.

16:45.295 --> 16:48.257
Mix it in and your magic lasts longer.

16:50.342 --> 16:53.012
What about the small bottle
on the opposite shelf?

16:53.095 --> 16:55.139
The white, sparkly one?

16:55.222 --> 16:57.766
That’s Blushing Bride Butterfly
scale powder.

16:57.850 --> 17:00.602
Add that and the ink turns transparent,

17:00.686 --> 17:02.771
so you can hide the lines of your seal.

17:02.855 --> 17:04.523
And next to that?

17:04.606 --> 17:07.317
The tall, narrow bottle
is Roaming Scallop powder.

17:07.818 --> 17:11.238
The round one beside it
is Golden Blaze Wyrm scale powder.

17:15.951 --> 17:17.286
Wow...

17:17.995 --> 17:20.039
That's amazing, Tartah!

17:20.497 --> 17:24.001
Do you really have all the names
of these dyes memorized?

17:24.084 --> 17:25.794
Well, they're our products.

17:26.336 --> 17:29.757
You're so lucky you get to live
in a magical supply shop!

17:29.840 --> 17:34.178
Just seeing all these shelves and bottles
lined up wall-to-wall gets me excited!

17:35.095 --> 17:38.182
I'm so envious of you, Tartah!

17:39.266 --> 17:42.269
The atelier’s obviously better.

17:43.103 --> 17:46.023
You're a witch.
That's a weird thing to say.

17:47.107 --> 17:50.194
Aren't you an apprentice too, Tartah?

17:51.612 --> 17:52.780
I'm...

17:56.283 --> 17:59.078
That red powder. What's that one called?

17:59.161 --> 18:00.120
Which one?

18:01.330 --> 18:03.082
That one! On that shelf!

18:08.170 --> 18:11.340
Between the pale blue
and the withered-leaf color!

18:11.423 --> 18:14.343
Which shelf and which row?

18:17.137 --> 18:20.015
It's really bright red. You can't miss it.

18:21.683 --> 18:22.518
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

18:29.566 --> 18:32.152
What was that light just now?

18:32.236 --> 18:34.279
That scared me.

18:34.363 --> 18:35.531
Are you okay?

18:39.910 --> 18:43.038
Thank goodness the bottles didn't break.

18:46.792 --> 18:48.043
No, this is bad.

18:48.836 --> 18:50.254
The worst.

18:51.547 --> 18:52.923
The labels came off.

18:53.006 --> 18:54.758
It's all mixed up.

18:55.259 --> 18:58.470
Gramps told me not to touch them.

18:58.554 --> 18:59.805
It's all a mess.

18:59.888 --> 19:03.559
I'm sorry! I'll help.
Let's put them all back.

19:04.143 --> 19:05.894
Do you know which powder is which?

19:08.397 --> 19:09.815
Which color to which ingred--

19:09.898 --> 19:11.316
I don't know!

19:12.484 --> 19:14.695
But earlier...

19:14.778 --> 19:17.698
I just memorized where they were placed.

19:17.781 --> 19:20.200
I didn’t recognize them by color.

19:28.125 --> 19:29.209
Sorry.

19:29.751 --> 19:31.336
Just go home.

19:31.920 --> 19:32.880
But...

19:35.299 --> 19:36.466
I hate to say it,

19:38.135 --> 19:40.721
but there’s nothing
you can do to help, Coco.

19:41.972 --> 19:44.808
There are things people can do
and things they can’t.

19:45.934 --> 19:47.853
With my Silverwash-diseased eyes,

19:48.353 --> 19:51.815
no matter how much I study,
I'll never be able to become a witch.

19:56.570 --> 19:58.530
See? I told you!

19:59.948 --> 20:01.992
Are you all right, Qifrey?

20:07.456 --> 20:11.543
That much power from such a tiny seal?

20:13.462 --> 20:16.590
I think this is the Twin Bottle spell.

20:18.133 --> 20:20.677
Two containers, one shared content.

20:21.220 --> 20:25.349
There’s probably a small medal engraved
with a seal sunk inside.

20:26.350 --> 20:28.560
Coco was made to use this.

20:29.603 --> 20:33.148
The ink kept refilling
with an unknown additive.

20:34.274 --> 20:37.236
This vial is connected to them.

20:39.488 --> 20:40.656
At last...

20:41.698 --> 20:43.200
I've finally found them.

20:43.909 --> 20:45.452
Good grief.

20:46.036 --> 20:48.038
A conjuring ink that can produce

20:48.121 --> 20:51.291
immense power
from such a crude, small ring?

20:52.918 --> 20:55.963
Something like that shouldn't exist
in this world.

20:56.672 --> 20:59.424
This is beyond me.

20:59.925 --> 21:01.843
We have to inform the Great Hall--

21:01.927 --> 21:03.220
We can't!

21:03.720 --> 21:07.766
We can't hand this over
to the Knights Moralis nor the Great Hall.

21:07.849 --> 21:11.603
It would be better
if no one knew we even discovered it.

21:15.315 --> 21:16.775
What are you saying?

21:18.360 --> 21:19.361
You...

21:20.153 --> 21:23.699
Do you understand what you're saying?

21:24.700 --> 21:26.118
What are you planning?

21:26.618 --> 21:29.079
What are you planning to do with that ink?

21:31.790 --> 21:34.251
I'm sorry, Mr. Nolnoa.

21:46.513 --> 21:47.514
Sorry to keep you waiting.

21:48.015 --> 21:50.267
About that conjuring ink vial,

21:51.268 --> 21:54.563
it seems he accidentally handed you
something very valuable.

21:55.147 --> 21:58.191
I bought you a bag to make up for it,
so you can use this.

21:58.275 --> 22:01.695
Wow, thank you so much!

22:15.667 --> 22:16.877
Master,

22:18.170 --> 22:20.839
what's Silverwash disease?

22:22.090 --> 22:23.592
The Silverwash syndrome

22:23.675 --> 22:25.677
is a condition you're born with.

22:26.178 --> 22:30.390
It makes the world look like
it's covered in silver.

22:31.725 --> 22:34.978
Witches tend to place importance
on eyesight,

22:35.062 --> 22:37.606
so it can make things difficult
in this world.

22:38.190 --> 22:42.235
Being so harsh on exceptions
is one of the witch's bad traits.

22:49.076 --> 22:51.370
Don't look so worried.

22:52.412 --> 22:53.622
It'll be okay.

22:54.206 --> 22:58.585
As long as you're a student of my atelier,
I'll do everything I can to protect you.

22:59.711 --> 23:02.756
There's nothing you have to worry about.

23:04.091 --> 23:05.133
Nothing.

23:08.845 --> 23:10.180
Gramps.

23:10.722 --> 23:14.267
I'm sorry.
The light earlier caught me by surprise,

23:14.351 --> 23:16.895
and I broke the bottles around here.

23:17.604 --> 23:20.357
What was that strong light?

23:20.857 --> 23:22.651
Mr. Qifrey's magic?

23:24.861 --> 23:27.030
Huh? Light?

23:29.616 --> 23:31.284
There was no light.

23:33.203 --> 23:34.287
Gramps?

23:34.371 --> 23:35.956
Subtitle translation by: Emily Noguchi

23:36.998 --> 23:40.961
EPISODE 9: NIGHTMARE SINKING INTO BLACK
